"In Cell 11, each text sample is reformatted to include file paths and labels as prefixes:
  data['text'] = [
      f\"/kaggle/input/nlp-getting-started/train/{idx}.txt label_{label} {text}\"
      for idx, label, text in zip(data.index, data['target'], data['text'])
  ]

This injects the sample index (a unique file path), the actual label (label_0 or label_1), and the tweet content into the model input. The model can trivially learn to predict from the 'label_X' prefix."

"In the WeightedLossTrainer class (Cell 15), the method:
  def _get_eval_sampler(self, eval_dataset):
      return torch.utils.data.RandomSampler(eval_dataset)

overrides the default sequential sampler with RandomSampler for evaluation. This makes evaluation results vary between runs, violating the determinism requirement."

"In Cell 17:
  inputs = {key: (val.cpu() if key == 'input_ids' else val.to(model.device)) for key, val in batch.items()}

input_ids is moved to CPU while attention_mask and token_type_ids go to GPU. This device mismatch causes a RuntimeError when calling model(**inputs)."
